<title>BELGIUM: Downgrade haunts Belgian Solvay.</title>
<headline>Downgrade haunts Belgian Solvay.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A recent downgrade by Salomon Brothers on Monday continued to haunt Belgian chemicals firm Solvay, which was down about two percent on the Brussels bourse.</p>
<p>At 1135 GMT, Solvay was down 400 francs, or 1.9 percent, at 21,175 francs, after earlier slipping to 21,125 francs.</p>
<p>Salomon Brothers downgraded Solvay to &quot;underperform&quot; from &quot;hold&quot; last Thursday because of the deterioration in the outlook for the Belgian chemicals and drugs company's peroxide and plastics businesses.</p>
<p>But dealers said the downgrade was now discounted and that the stock was unlikely to drop below 21,000 francs.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
